Language":"Shall the City of Bowlus adopt Optional Plan A, modifying the standard plan of City government to an elected Mayor and four elected City Council members, with the City Clerk and City Treasurer to be appointed by the City Council?","mcds":["07066"]},{"id":"mn-morrison-14356-township-question-1-cushing-twp","name":"TOWNSHIP QUESTION 1 (Cushing Twp): Appointment of Town Clerk and Treasurer","type":"Local Public Question","statewide":false,"ballotLanguage":"Shall Option B, providing for the appointment of a town clerk and treasurer by the town board, be adopted for the government of Cushing Township?","mcds":["14356"]},{"id":"mn-morrison-sd0181-school-district-question-1-isd-181","name":"SCHOOL DISTRICT QUESTION 1 (ISD #181): Approval of New School District Referendum Revenue Authorization","type":"Local Public Question","statewide":false,"ballotLanguage":"The school board of Independent School District No. 181 (Brainerd Public Schools) has proposed to increase its general education revenue by $865 per pupil. The proposed referendum revenue authorization would be applicable for ten years beginning with taxes payable in 2027, and increase each year by the rate of inflation beginning with taxes payable in 2028, unless otherwise revoked or reduced as provided by law.\n\nShall the increase in the revenue proposed by the school board of Independent School District No. 181 be approved?\n\nBY VOTING \"YES\" ON THIS BALLOT QUESTION, YOU ARE VOTING FOR A PROPERTY TAX INCREASE.","schoolNum":"0181","area":"Brainerd"}]}